WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.511 --> 00:00:18.194
king's men hurried to Saint Albans, but Robin wasn't there.

2
00:00:19.215 --> 00:00:22.137
The Bishop of Hereford soon joined the king's men.

3
00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:26.141
"The king put me in charge," announced the bishop.

4
00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:29.004
He divided the men into small groups.

5
00:00:30.688 --> 00:00:32.710
They searched the countryside for Robin.

6
00:00:33.831 --> 00:00:35.732
They blocked every road and path.

7
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:38.755
But there was no sign of Robin.

8
00:00:40.396 --> 00:00:43.819
Then the Sheriff of Nottingham and all his men joined the bishop.

9
00:00:43.839 --> 00:00:48.123
"I look forward to capturing Robin," said the sheriff.

10
00:00:48.143 --> 00:00:49.924
"So do I!"

11
00:00:50.345 --> 00:00:51.045
said the bishop.

12
00:00:52.466 --> 00:00:55.209
Meanwhile Robin had been walking for days.

13
00:00:55.969 --> 00:00:58.892
He whistled as he walked along the road, unworried.

14
00:00:59.644 --> 00:01:03.205
Then he paused at a stream to wash his face and get a drink of water.

15
00:01:03.645 --> 00:01:06.026
Suddenly something whizzed past his ear!

16
00:01:06.046 --> 00:01:08.087
"An arrow!"

17
00:01:08.527 --> 00:01:09.227
cried Robin.

18
00:01:09.947 --> 00:01:13.908
He sprang to his feet and raced through the stream and into the dense woods.

19
00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:17.670
The king's men galloped after him until they reached the woods.

20
00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.191
Then they left their horses and ran after him.

21
00:01:21.711 --> 00:01:25.012
But Robin knew the area much better than the king's men did.

22
00:01:25.824 --> 00:01:31.068
He crawled along the ground, and then stooped and ran, until finally he escaped the men.

23
00:01:32.589 --> 00:01:35.831
Panting, he finally stopped at the top of a hill.

24
00:01:37.553 --> 00:01:40.134
Below he saw even more of the king's men.

25
00:01:40.154 --> 00:01:42.336
"I need a disguise!"

26
00:01:42.756 --> 00:01:44.358
Robin's stomach growled.

27
00:01:44.378 --> 00:01:46.179
"And some food!"

28
00:01:46.799 --> 00:01:50.362
Robin was careful to stay hidden as he walked toward Nottingham.

29
00:01:51.022 --> 00:01:52.904
He soon spotted a shoemaker.

30
00:01:55.036 --> 00:01:55.697
"Hello, there!"

31
00:01:56.057 --> 00:01:56.757
Robin called.

32
00:01:56.777 --> 00:01:58.959
"I was admiring your outfit.

33
00:01:59.359 --> 00:02:00.620
Will you change clothes with me?

34
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.022
And share your lunch?"

35
00:02:03.042 --> 00:02:04.202
The shoemaker laughed.

36
00:02:04.222 --> 00:02:07.625
"Your clothes are much nicer than mine.

37
00:02:08.465 --> 00:02:10.066
Why do you want to change?"

38
00:02:10.086 --> 00:02:13.088
"I'm playing a joke on someone."

39
00:02:13.489 --> 00:02:14.850
Robin held out his hand.

40
00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.952
"Here, I'll give you ten gold coins."

41
00:02:17.972 --> 00:02:19.473
"All right!"

42
00:02:21.094 --> 00:02:23.776
The two men changed clothes and sat down to eat.

43
00:02:24.492 --> 00:02:28.195
They were exchanging stories when the king's men suddenly interrupted them.

44
00:02:28.215 --> 00:02:30.636
"There he is!"

45
00:02:31.137 --> 00:02:32.057
one of the men called.

46
00:02:32.077 --> 00:02:34.459
"Robin Hood, you're under arrest!"

47
00:02:34.799 --> 00:02:36.340
said another man to the shoemaker.

48
00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.221
"I'm not Robin Hood!"

49
00:02:38.702 --> 00:02:39.582
said the shoemaker.

50
00:02:40.123 --> 00:02:42.644
But the king's men didn't listen to the shoemaker.

51
00:02:43.325 --> 00:02:46.727
They tied his hands behind him and then took him away.

52
00:02:47.828 --> 00:02:49.849
Robin knew the shoemaker would be all right.

53
00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.972
The bishop would quickly realize the shoemaker wasn't Robin.

54
00:02:55.452 --> 00:02:56.993
So Robin continued walking.

55
00:02:57.473 --> 00:02:59.653
But by dark, he was exhausted.

56
00:02:59.673 --> 00:03:03.294
"I'd better get some sleep," Robin thought.

57
00:03:03.975 --> 00:03:08.576
He stopped at the next inn along the road and got one of the last available beds.

58
00:03:09.156 --> 00:03:12.477
He fell asleep almost before his head touched the pillow.

59
00:03:13.858 --> 00:03:17.959
When Robin awoke at dawn, he found a friar sleeping in the next bed.

60
00:03:18.619 --> 00:03:20.880
Quickly he dressed in the friar's clothes.

61
00:03:21.564 --> 00:03:24.645
Outside he took the friar's mule and hurried away.

62
00:03:25.106 --> 00:03:29.347
Disguised as a friar, Robin passed right by some of the king's men.

63
00:03:30.548 --> 00:03:34.590
As Robin rode down a lane, he spotted a familiar knight.

64
00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:38.471
"Sir Richard, how nice to see you!"

65
00:03:38.831 --> 00:03:41.132
exclaimed Robin, leaping off the mule.

66
00:03:41.793 --> 00:03:42.833
"I've been on the run."

67
00:03:43.673 --> 00:03:46.054
He told Sir Richard about the men chasing him.

68
00:03:46.074 --> 00:03:49.756
"But I'll soon be safely back in Sherwood Forest."

69
00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.845
Sir Richard shook his head.

70
00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:54.926
"You're in great danger, Robin.

71
00:03:55.546 --> 00:03:57.607
Everyone knows you're disguised as a friar.

72
00:03:58.047 --> 00:03:59.027
There's only one thing to do.

73
00:03:59.568 --> 00:04:01.849
Go back to London and ask for Queen Eleanor's help."

74
00:04:01.869 --> 00:04:04.110
"Back to London?"

75
00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.631
Robin felt his heart sink.

76
00:04:06.651 --> 00:04:09.492
"Yes, come with me," Sir Richard said.

77
00:04:09.512 --> 00:04:11.433
"You can dress as one of my men.

78
00:04:11.953 --> 00:04:13.313
We'll travel with you to London."

79
00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:18.936
Robin didn't want to go back to London, but Sir Richard was a very wise knight.

80
00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.883
So Robin changed his clothes once again and followed Sir Richard.

81
00:04:25.505 --> 00:04:30.328
Queen Eleanor was walking in her garden among the roses when a man leaped over the wall.

82
00:04:30.929 --> 00:04:34.752
He hung onto the wall for a moment before dropping lightly on the grass.

83
00:04:35.332 --> 00:04:38.915
Her maids shrieked, but the queen recognized Robin.

84
00:04:38.935 --> 00:04:41.077
"Your Majesty!"

85
00:04:41.677 --> 00:04:43.039
Robin knelt at her feet.

86
00:04:43.059 --> 00:04:46.101
"Help! The king's men are after me."

87
00:04:46.121 --> 00:04:49.484
"What?" The queen looked furious.

88
00:04:50.264 --> 00:04:52.685
"The king has broken his promise.

89
00:04:53.366 --> 00:04:54.847
He won't get away with this!

90
00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:56.667
Wait here, Robin."

91
00:04:58.669 --> 00:05:00.329
Queen Eleanor returned soon.

92
00:05:00.349 --> 00:05:02.931
"You can travel safely, Robin.

93
00:05:04.111 --> 00:05:07.293
The king has promised me again that you will be safe."

94
00:05:08.314 --> 00:05:11.275
Robin saw that her eyes were still bright with anger.

95
00:05:11.295 --> 00:05:15.617
"And this time he will not break his promise!"

96
00:05:16.998 --> 00:05:19.920
After three days Robin set off for home again.

97
00:05:20.872 --> 00:05:26.517
Along the way he passed many of the king's men, but this time no one dared to harm

98
00:05:26.557 --> 00:05:39.808
him. At last Robin arrived safely back in Sherwood And there he stayed for many years with his

99
00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:44.212
merry men, singing, feasting, and shooting his bow and arrow.
